You can install Appium (Appium 2.x/3.x CLI, plus the uiautomator2 and xcuitest drivers and appium-doctor) on Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) via npm.

1. Install Node.js/npm & Android Platform Tools (adb) via APT

(If you don't already have npm installed, run this first; otherwise skip straight to step 2.)
bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y nodejs npm adb default-jdk
Use code with caution.

2. Install Appium, appium-doctor, & Automation Drivers via npm

bash
# 1. Install Appium globally
sudo npm install -g appium appium-doctor

# 2. Install the Android (UiAutomator2) driver into your user's APPIUM_HOME (~/.appium)
appium driver install uiautomator2
Use code with caution.
(Note: Ensure ANDROID_HOME is exported in your ~/.bashrc—for example, export ANDROID_HOME=$HOME/Android/Sdk and export PATH=$PATH:$ANDROID_HOME/platform-tools—so Appium can locate adb and apksigner.)

3. Verify Appium & Installed Drivers Are Ready

bash
for tool in appium appium-doctor adb java; do
  if command -v "$tool" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "✅ $tool -> $(command -v "$tool")"
  else
    echo "❌ $tool -> MISSING"
  fi
done

appium --version
appium driver list --installed
Use code with caution.
